1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,547
So our gathering today has a name,

2
00:00:02,547 --> 00:00:04,311
and it's called "Your Sins Are Forgiven."

3
00:00:04,311 --> 00:00:06,662
You might find that a bit abrupt —

4
00:00:06,662 --> 00:00:07,838
our very first time meeting,

5
00:00:07,838 --> 00:00:10,189
so why talk about your sins being forgiven?

6
00:00:10,189 --> 00:00:11,757
Now, there's a picture next to me,

7
00:00:11,757 --> 00:00:12,933
an image beside me,

8
00:00:12,933 --> 00:00:14,500
and that image, in fact,

9
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,460
comes from this book right here.

10
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:19,007
I don't know if you can see, here in my hand,

11
00:00:19,007 --> 00:00:20,770
I'm holding this book right now.

12
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:21,946
And this book —

13
00:00:21,946 --> 00:00:24,298
well, I doubt many people could read it,

14
00:00:24,298 --> 00:00:26,845
because it's written in Nepali.

15
00:00:26,845 --> 00:00:29,392
I bought it over in Kathmandu,

16
00:00:29,392 --> 00:00:29,980
and so,

17
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,380
this here is an event from the Lord Jesus' life on earth.

18
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:37,160
We'll have a chance to talk about it a little later.

19
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:42,280
Just now, after you heard Killy,

20
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,940
and after you heard Sai-fai share,

21
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:46,380
I wonder if you envy the change in their lives.

22
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:50,920
It makes me think of this one verse in the Bible.

23
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:51,840
What does it say?

24
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,420
It is the One who girds us with strength,

25
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:56,880
and makes our way perfect;

26
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:57,480
He is God.

27
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:03,120
The God we come to know today isn't just a doctrine — He is a living Person.

28
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:06,440
Some people say you become like the company you keep.

29
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:12,320
You'll find that those who believe in God have changed lives, real experiences,

30
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:17,960
and they change for the better. From this you see God is not only real, but good.

31
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:22,560
He is the One who girds us with strength and makes our way perfect.

32
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:27,560
And I hope that today, through coming to know this God,

33
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,560
your life, too, will be changed like this.

34
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:35,560
On my desk there's an ornament

35
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:38,560
that constantly reminds me how real God is.

36
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:42,560
Can you see what I'm holding in my hand?

37
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,560
It might be a little dark.

38
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:50,560
It's actually a magnetically levitating globe.

39
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:53,560
Sometimes I buy little things as gifts to myself,

40
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:57,560
and this globe — what does it remind me of?

41
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:04,560
Well, long ago many people believed the earth was flat.

42
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:08,560
In fact, to this day there's even an International Flat Earth Society

43
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:11,560
that claims the earth is flat.

44
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,560
So the people of old used to say

45
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,560
that sailing the seas and racing horses each carry their risks.

46
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,560
Why is that?

47
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,560
Why was sailing so dangerous?

48
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,560
Because they thought the earth was flat.

49
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,060
If you went too far out,

50
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:24,560
you would fall off the edge,

51
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,560
tumbling down like off a waterfall.

52
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,560
So the seafarers of old

53
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:31,060
would hug the coastline as they went,

54
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:33,060
sailing a while, then back to shore,

55
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,060
a while more, then back to shore,

56
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:35,560
never daring to cross the open ocean,

57
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:38,560
because they feared falling off that waterfall.

58
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,560
And you'll notice —

59
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,560
when did people finally realize

60
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,560
that the earth is actually round?

61
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,560
Well, going back to this,

62
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,060
you see there are two pictures here.

63
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:52,060
Going back to the Greek era,

64
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:54,460
back to around 200 or 300 BC,

65
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:56,660
some people began to wonder and to reason.

66
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:57,060
What was it?

67
00:02:57,060 --> 00:02:57,460


68
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:59,260
when they watched a lunar eclipse,

69
00:02:59,260 --> 00:02:59,760


70
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:01,360
there was a shadow on the moon.

71
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,060
That is —

72
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:04,260
the earth was blocking the sun,

73
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:06,260
and the shadow it cast had a curve to it.

74
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:06,560


75
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:09,060
so they guessed the earth was curved.

76
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:09,560


77
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,060
For instance, there were others who noticed something as well,

78
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:11,560
and it was this —

79
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,860
that on one and the very same day,

80
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:14,660
yet in two different places,

81
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:19,000
the shadows cast by the sun were not the same at all.

82
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:22,420
Over in Egypt, the shadow would fall perfectly straight down,

83
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,380
but a few hundred miles further away,

84
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,700
that very same shadow fell at a slant, at an angle.

85
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:29,760
And from that, they guessed that the earth must be curved.

86
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:33,600
But when was it that people finally proved the earth really is round?

87
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:35,900
It wasn't until the Middle Ages, right around the 16th century.

88
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:40,260
So why is it that Columbus and Magellan became so famous?

89
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:44,360
It's because their discoveries were made at the genuine risk of their very lives.

90
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:52,360
Because out on an ocean voyage, if the earth really had been flat, they would set sail and never be able to turn back again.

91
00:03:52,360 --> 00:04:00,360
But as it turns out, the Bible has a verse that says exactly this, over in the book of Isaiah —

92
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:06,716
And when was the book of Isaiah written? It was around the 700s BC,

93
00:04:06,716 --> 00:04:09,649
roughly the time of China's Eastern Zhou dynasty,

94
00:04:09,649 --> 00:04:11,360
even earlier than the Spring and Autumn period.

95
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:17,360
The Bible says this: God sits enthroned above the circle of the earth.

96
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:22,360
So the Bible told us this long, long ago — 2,700 years ago it had already told us

97
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:25,360
that the earth is a great circle.

98
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:32,360
And the original word even carries the sense of something solid, something three-dimensional.

99
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:36,360
That's why some English versions render it as "the sphere of the earth,"

100
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:40,360
meaning upon the round globe of the earth itself.

101
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,359
Here's another example.

102
00:04:41,359 --> 00:04:45,853
People long ago thought the earth must be hung up by something,

103
00:04:45,853 --> 00:04:47,601
held up by something,

104
00:04:47,601 --> 00:04:50,348
because if nothing were hanging it,

105
00:04:50,348 --> 00:04:52,096
nothing holding it up,

106
00:04:52,096 --> 00:04:53,594
it would just keep falling.

107
00:04:53,594 --> 00:04:57,839
But do any of you feel like you're falling? No.

108
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:00,087
So surely something must be hanging it,

109
00:05:00,087 --> 00:05:01,585
something holding it up.

110
00:05:01,585 --> 00:05:05,580
So you'll find that in myths all over the world,

111
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,443
there are legends just like this.

112
00:05:07,443 --> 00:05:10,238
Some picture the earth carried on a turtle,

113
00:05:10,238 --> 00:05:11,868
some on a great elephant,

114
00:05:11,868 --> 00:05:13,498
some on the shoulders of a strongman.

115
00:05:13,498 --> 00:05:16,526
Maybe, who knows, after holding it up so long,

116
00:05:16,526 --> 00:05:17,691
he shifts a little,

117
00:05:17,691 --> 00:05:19,321
and then you get an earthquake.

118
00:05:19,321 --> 00:05:20,718
That's how it is in the myths,

119
00:05:20,718 --> 00:05:23,280
in the human imagination.

120
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:26,899
But the Bible tells us it isn't so.

121
00:05:26,899 --> 00:05:32,328
The book of Job is even older than the Isaiah we just mentioned,

122
00:05:32,328 --> 00:05:37,153
perhaps 3,500 to 4,000 years ago,

123
00:05:37,153 --> 00:05:42,280
around 1,500 to 2,000 BC.

124
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,620
And the Bible has this verse:

125
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:46,748
He stretches out the north over empty space,

126
00:05:46,748 --> 00:05:48,663
and hangs the earth on nothing.

127
00:05:48,663 --> 00:05:50,152
The Chinese doesn't quite capture it,

128
00:05:50,152 --> 00:05:52,280
so how does the English put it?

129
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,280
What does it say?

130
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:57,280
It says God "hangs the earth on nothing."

131
00:05:57,280 --> 00:06:00,280
That is, God hung the earth without anything holding it up.

132
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:02,280
Isn't that remarkable?

133
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:07,280
So let me ask you: when did we learn the earth truly hangs on nothing, held up by nothing?

134
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:10,280
When did the solid proof actually come?

135
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:13,280
Not until rockets rose into space.

136
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:15,280
And when the astronauts finally looked back at the earth, what did they find?

137
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,280
Why, there really was no great elephant down there,

138
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:20,280
and truly no strongman's shoulders holding it up at all.

139
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:24,262
And on top of all that, there were the great expeditions to the North Pole,

140
00:06:24,262 --> 00:06:25,348
and the expeditions down to the South Pole as well.

141
00:06:25,348 --> 00:06:27,339
Even the very farthest places on earth were finally reached,

142
00:06:27,339 --> 00:06:28,606
and still they found no rope anywhere,

143
00:06:28,606 --> 00:06:29,873
nothing hanging it up,

144
00:06:29,873 --> 00:06:31,140
and nothing holding it up from below.

145
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:33,568
Yet already, more than three or four thousand years ago,

146
00:06:33,568 --> 00:06:35,129
the Bible had told us this very thing:

147
00:06:35,129 --> 00:06:35,476
that God —

148
00:06:35,476 --> 00:06:40,680
"He hangs the earth on nothing."

149
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:43,539
And here is yet another verse.

150
00:06:43,539 --> 00:06:47,668
It says: Have you, in your days, commanded the morning,

151
00:06:47,668 --> 00:06:49,892
and caused the dawn

152
00:06:49,892 --> 00:06:51,480
to know its place,

153
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:57,680
so that by this light the earth is changed like clay under the seal?

154
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:59,280
Now what on earth does that mean?

155
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:03,247
Well, it's describing that very moment of sunrise early in the morning,

156
00:07:03,247 --> 00:07:05,797
as the ground slowly grows brighter and brighter,

157
00:07:05,797 --> 00:07:09,480
and the light spreads across it like a seal being pressed into clay.

158
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,480
What am I even talking about?

159
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:17,480
Do you know how people in the old days used to make a seal impression?

160
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:24,480
They would carve their patterns and letters onto a round stone cylinder,

161
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:29,480
then they would prepare a flat, smooth surface of clay,

162
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:32,480
and roll that cylinder right across the clay.

163
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:36,480
And after the pressing, don't all the patterns and letters come out onto it?

164
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:40,129
And that same stone seal could then be used to print a second time,

165
00:07:40,129 --> 00:07:41,345
and even a third time after that.

166
00:07:41,345 --> 00:07:45,480
That's exactly how the people back then made all their impressions.

167
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:50,980
So why would the sunrise be likened to a seal on clay? What is it really picturing for us?

168
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:55,480
You notice how it grows brighter and brighter, the darkness slowly receding away,

169
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:59,480
and the changing of the whole earth is just like that rolling seal,

170
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:05,480
as if to show us that the earth, like a rolling seal, actually turns — it rotates on its own axis.

171
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:08,371
And not only does the earth rotate,

172
00:08:08,371 --> 00:08:10,849
it also happens to tilt —

173
00:08:10,849 --> 00:08:13,740
tilted over at 23.5 degrees.

174
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:20,840
And what effect does that have? Well, it's because of that very 23.5-degree tilt that we get spring, summer, autumn, and winter.

175
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:22,752
So in just a couple of days from now,

176
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:25,301
it will be the winter solstice up in the Northern Hemisphere,

177
00:08:25,301 --> 00:08:30,080
while down in the Southern Hemisphere it may well be the longest day of the entire year.

178
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:33,580
Now don't the four seasons make life so much more colorful?

179
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:35,580
And they serve a very practical purpose too,

180
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:37,830
because when the earth is tilted on its axis like this,

181
00:08:37,830 --> 00:08:41,080
you find that many more regions become warmer,

182
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,830
and far more livable for people,

183
00:08:42,830 --> 00:08:46,580
so the habitable areas of the world increase a great deal.

184
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:53,580
If it spun straight up with no tilt at all, the middle would be scorching hot and the poles freezing cold.

185
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:59,580
So why is the Bible so utterly extraordinary?

186
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:04,580
It says so very much about the earth and about science,

187
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:06,580
so why on earth is it so remarkably accurate?

188
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:09,580
Even running ahead of what so many would only later discover,

189
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:13,580
things that could only be proven with hard evidence many years afterward.

190
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:16,580
It's because the Bible is the very word of God.

191
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:18,580
Just as the Bible says here,

192
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:20,580
All Scripture is breathed out by God.

193
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:22,580
The Bible is the word of God.

194
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:29,580
This heaven and earth was made by God, so of course He knows every detail of it,

195
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:34,580
and so through the Bible God lets us come to know these things.

196
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:40,580
So through all we've said, you can know the One in the Bible is the true God,

197
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:45,580
and through the Bible we also come to know how real the true God is.

198
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:48,660
And it's not only through the Bible.

199
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:54,020
You'll notice — when you have time, why do people love to travel, to head out into nature?

200
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,300
Because it's beautiful.

201
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:58,640
When you take in the created world, you find it is —

202
00:09:58,900 --> 00:09:59,920
so grand,

203
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:01,460
so wonderful,

204
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,240
so intricate,

205
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:04,780
so beautiful.

206
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:11,180
The Bible has a verse — what does it say? It says: ever since the creation of the world,

207
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:12,980
God's eternal power

208
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:14,260
His everlasting power

209
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:17,080
and His divine nature — that is, what He is like —

210
00:10:17,340 --> 00:10:18,860
are clearly seen.

211
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:20,920
Though unseen by the eye,

212
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:22,960
yet through the things He has made

213
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:24,240
they can be understood,

214
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:26,040
leaving people without excuse.

215
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:31,420
So through the created world — the more you go outdoors and look around,

216
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:33,200
you'll come to know God too. Why?

217
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:35,760
Because you see the world, and isn't it wonderful?

218
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:38,840
It's like this watch you see in my hand right now.

219
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,900
When you look at the watch, isn't it beautifully made?

220
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:44,900
Surely someone designed it, someone built it.

221
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:48,900
And the beauty of this world, its intricacy,

222
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:50,900
is far more complex than this watch.

223
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,900
So when I look at this world,

224
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:56,900
I know there truly is a Designer, a Creator.

225
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:59,900
And God truly did create all things.

226
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:04,900
Now there was once a survey

227
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:08,900
of some of the most eminent scientists of the last few centuries.

228
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:10,900
What did that survey find?

229
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:16,900
Among the scientists surveyed, over ninety percent believed in God.

230
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:22,900
So let me tell you — believing in God is not rejecting science.

231
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:25,900
More than ninety percent of those scientists believed there is a God.

232
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:29,900
Why? Because the more they researched, the more they understood this world,

233
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:32,900
the more they realized there must be a Designer, a Creator.

234
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:35,900
So believing in God today is in fact very reasonable.

235
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:42,300
This study was even published in the newspapers.

236
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:45,620
I wonder if you happened to notice the news.

237
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:49,460
As we come to this point,

238
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:53,560
you'll find that the God we are speaking of today,

239
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:55,860
the God recorded in the Bible,

240
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:57,920
is the Creator of heaven, earth, and all things.

241
00:11:57,920 --> 00:11:59,460
He is not made by human hands.

242
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:03,040
As someone once put it, the true God is the One who made man,

243
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:04,060
who made heaven, earth, and all things.

244
00:12:04,060 --> 00:12:06,620
A false god is made by man.

245
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:10,200
And the Bible says false gods have eyes

246
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,740
but cannot see,

247
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:13,280
have ears but cannot hear,

248
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,820
have mouths but cannot speak.

249
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:18,900
They can't be bought or sold in the market,

250
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,220
and they never go on sale.

251
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:25,300
And besides, you just heard Killy's testimony a moment ago,

252
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,580
and you heard Sai-fai's testimony as well,

253
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:29,400
and you could see from them that God really is kind, and that He is good.

254
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:37,280
Now some people — say, those in the triads, the gangs — will worship idols and false gods.

255
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:42,320
The gangsters will pray that all their whoring, their gambling, and their drinking go along smoothly.

256
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:46,480
And funnily enough, the police station right there worships the very same idol.

257
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:50,480
So the next time your robbery happens to fail,

258
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:55,960
you might just want to wonder whether the very god you worship tipped them off — whether he turned informant on you.

259
00:12:55,960 --> 00:13:02,960
So from all of this you can clearly see: this God is the Creator of heaven and all things, and He is truly good.

260
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:10,960
The Bible lets us know this: that God is love.

261
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:16,960
God so greatly desires that people would receive all of His goodness, and all of His riches.

262
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:22,960
And so He sent His only begotten Son — God sent His one and only Son —

263
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:27,960
in order to let people come to know Him, and to help them.

264
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:30,560
Now concerning the Lord Jesus coming into the world —

265
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:33,560
there are a great many prophecies about it in the Bible.

266
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,260
And as the word itself suggests, a prophecy is —

267
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:38,840
something that has not yet happened at all,

268
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,160
and yet is foretold and announced in advance.

269
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:43,420
In fact, concerning the Lord Jesus' birth,

270
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:47,120
the Bible foretold the very time when He would come,

271
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,840
and the very place where He would be born,

272
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:50,040
and even what He was coming to do —

273
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:52,420
over three hundred such prophecies in all.

274
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:54,640
Their purpose is to let us know,

275
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,340
so that when the Lord Jesus came,

276
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:57,400
we would not mistake Him.

277
00:13:57,400 --> 00:14:00,020
He is the Savior God sent.

278
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:02,020
He is the Son of God.

279
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:04,020
Here is one example.

280
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:09,020
We know that at Christmas, coming soon,

281
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:11,020
where was the Lord Jesus born?

282
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:14,020
In Bethlehem of Israel.

283
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:17,020
Now in the Old Testament book of Micah,

284
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:20,020
around the 700s BC —

285
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:23,020
that is, some seven hundred years before the Lord Jesus was born —

286
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:25,020
there was already a saying like this.

287
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:26,020
What does it say?

288
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:29,020
It says: But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah,

289
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:31,840
though you are little among the towns of Judah,

290
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:33,620
out of you shall come One

291
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:34,900
who will come forth for Me,

292
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:37,220
to be the ruler

293
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:38,500
in Israel,

294
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:40,020
whose origins

295
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:41,560
are from of old,

296
00:14:41,820 --> 00:14:42,840
from ancient times.

297
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,640
These two lines say it very clearly.

298
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:46,420
"Bethlehem Ephrathah" —

299
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:50,520
"little among the towns of Judah" — so it's a town, a place.

300
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:54,100
Bethlehem was originally a very small town,

301
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:57,440
but a King would come forth from it,

302
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:59,880
to be the ruler in Israel.

303
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:02,320
A king coming forth — that alone isn't so strange.

304
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:06,260
Even a king emerging, small as the town is —

305
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:09,540
a small town producing a king isn't strange.

306
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:10,760
That could well happen.

307
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:12,760
But notice the very last line.

308
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:14,460
It says His origins

309
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:18,440
have existed from the very beginning.

310
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:22,020
Apart from God, who could meet this condition?

311
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:24,840
Only the self-existent, eternal God

312
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,620
could meet it.

313
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:32,000
So from this one verse we know that Bethlehem would see not merely some king appear,

314
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,780
but rather, what kind of King would it be?

315
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:39,940
It would be the Son of God Himself entering the world, the One whose origins are from all eternity.

316
00:15:42,740 --> 00:15:45,060
Now when the Lord Jesus came to this earth,

317
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:47,860
He went all about the land doing good,

318
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:49,400
and He performed a great many miracles,

319
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:51,200
and He helped so very many people.

320
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:54,020
He opened the eyes of the blind

321
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:55,540
and made them able to see once again.

322
00:15:55,540 --> 00:16:00,540
And I wonder, at this very stage of your own life,

323
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:04,540
just how much you have really come to understand about living.

324
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:07,540
Are you perhaps still groping your way about in the dark,

325
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:08,540
still feeling lost and adrift,

326
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:11,540
not knowing what the meaning of life really is,

327
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:13,540
not even knowing what it is you're chasing after?

328
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:16,540
The Lord Jesus came and gave sight to the blind,

329
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:18,540
and in the same way He brings real light into our lives.

330
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:23,540
He also once stood up and stilled the very wind and the waves in the midst of a storm.

331
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:26,100
He is able to rescue our lives from danger,

332
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,140
and He is just as able to calm the raging storm.

333
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:31,740
In your life you will sometimes meet with circumstances

334
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:33,780
that press in hard upon you like a fierce storm,

335
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:35,580
leaving you anxious and unsettled,

336
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:37,880
and making you feel as though you're in real danger.

337
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:40,940
But the Lord is well able to help you,

338
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:43,260
calming every last storm within your heart,

339
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,540
and carrying you safely through it all.

340
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:46,840
He was also able to make

341
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,620
the lame man get up and walk.

342
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:54,000
And He cast out many unclean spirits, setting free all those who were possessed by demons.

343
00:16:54,000 --> 00:17:00,140
Perhaps some of you feel that your lives are bound up tightly by so very many things —

344
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:05,260
some bad old habits, perhaps a foul temper,

345
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:09,860
an unhealthy way of living, or certain sins,

346
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:15,760
some perhaps even troubled by evil spirits — and you'll find that the Lord is able to help with all of it, and to set you free.

347
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:22,760
He even once raised the dead back to life, giving life itself back to people.

348
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:28,760
So besides fulfilling so many of the Bible's prophecies,

349
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:32,760
and showing us plainly that He is the Savior God had promised to send,

350
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:37,312
through the very things that the Lord Jesus actually did,

351
00:17:37,312 --> 00:17:43,760
we also come to know that He is the very One God was sending.

352
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:48,760
Now at the very beginning I mentioned this little book here.

353
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:51,760
So what story is it that this little book actually tells?

354
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:55,760
Well, it tells of a paralyzed man, and his own experience of being healed,

355
00:17:55,760 --> 00:17:59,760
and it's recorded for us in the Gospel of Mark.

356
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,760
So what exactly happened in this account?

357
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:06,760
At the time, the Lord Jesus had come to a place called Capernaum.

358
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:09,760
And from this detail too you can see that the Bible is real and true.

359
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:14,120
It doesn't just say "long, long ago, in a land far, far away,"

360
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,640
all vague and dreamlike like that — no, not at all.

361
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:17,440
The actual place the Lord Jesus came to

362
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:19,240
was right on the north shore of the Sea of Galilee,

363
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:20,760
in the region of a town called Capernaum.

364
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:26,920
By then the Lord had already done many signs and wonders, so many had been helped, and His fame had spread far and wide.

365
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:31,780
He went into a certain house, and so many people came to Him that they crowded in all around Him,

366
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,340
until there was no room left anywhere, not even outside at the door.

367
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:39,720
And there was a certain paralyzed man — paralyzed, meaning that he simply couldn't walk at all.

368
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:45,760
But here's the precious part — he happened to have four friends, four men who carried him along.

369
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:51,760
The paralyzed man lay there upon his mat, completely unable to move himself,

370
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:53,760
and I find this detail really quite meaningful.

371
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:57,760
I wonder if you've ever noticed that sometimes a person's whole life

372
00:18:57,760 --> 00:19:01,760
is ruled entirely by his circumstances, as though he can't govern himself at all —

373
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:04,760
wherever that mat happens to be carried, that is exactly where he goes.

374
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:12,160
So the four friends each took hold of a corner and carried the paralytic right before the Lord,

375
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:14,360
all of them hoping that the Lord would be able to help them.

376
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:17,360
But there were so very many people there that they simply couldn't get into the house,

377
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:21,560
and so they climbed up onto the roof and tore the roof open.

378
00:19:21,560 --> 00:19:28,360
Then they lowered the paralytic down, mat and all, right down before the Lord.

379
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:33,360
Now you might well say — were they really allowed to do a thing like that?

380
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:38,360
So let me show you what daily life was actually like for people back in those days.

381
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:41,360
The houses that people lived in looked something rather like this.

382
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:44,360
Notice that the roof is only one story up off the ground,

383
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:48,360
and that the roof was usually quite flat, used for drying things out.

384
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:53,360
And there was a staircase on the outside leading right up to the roof.

385
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:58,360
So the four men carried the paralyzed man all the way up onto the roof.

386
00:19:58,360 --> 00:20:01,360
And what exactly were those roofs made of?

387
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:09,360
Well, back then they were very simple: just a few wooden beams laid across, covered over with branches and straw, and then a layer of clay on top of that.

388
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:12,703
So after every single rain,

389
00:20:12,703 --> 00:20:14,760
they would have to take a heavy stone roller

390
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:16,560
and roll it over to flatten the roof out again,

391
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:18,360
and then leave it to dry out in the sun.

392
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:24,360
So from this you can understand how they were able to tear open the roof and dig their way through it.

393
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:26,920
And by the way, let me mention this in passing —

394
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:28,460
you know, in English

395
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,000
there's a particular saying:

396
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:33,580
when it really pours, people say it's "raining cats and dogs."

397
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:35,880
Now what does that have to do with cats and dogs?

398
00:20:36,140 --> 00:20:37,420
Well, it comes from something rather like this.

399
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:41,760
Because back then, people's roofs were usually topped with straw,

400
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,560
all laid across the top like this.

401
00:20:43,820 --> 00:20:45,860
And many animals — the cats and the dogs —

402
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:47,920
would make their home up inside that straw.

403
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:49,440
So whenever it rained really hard,

404
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:51,760
they would all come washing and sliding down off the roof.

405
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:56,400
And that's the very reason heavy rain came to be called "raining cats and dogs."

406
00:20:56,400 --> 00:21:01,760
So they tore open the roof and lowered the man down through it.

407
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:08,000
And what was it that the Lord said?

408
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:12,000
The Lord saw their faith — now notice that carefully, their faith.

409
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:16,000
And that means not only the paralytic, but the four friends as well.

410
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:20,000
So why was it that He saw their faith?

411
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,028
Because you can plainly see what it was they believed.

412
00:21:23,028 --> 00:21:26,756
They believed that if they could only bring the paralytic before the Lord,

413
00:21:26,756 --> 00:21:28,386
there would surely be real hope for him.

414
00:21:28,386 --> 00:21:29,784
They believed the Lord would be able to help,

415
00:21:29,784 --> 00:21:32,579
and so they even went so far as to tear open the roof —

416
00:21:32,579 --> 00:21:35,142
at worst, they could repair it for the owner afterward,

417
00:21:35,142 --> 00:21:38,170
and they didn't fear the risk of being scolded for it.

418
00:21:38,170 --> 00:21:40,267
Braving the very real chance of a sharp rebuke,

419
00:21:40,267 --> 00:21:44,460
they still tore open that roof to lower the paralytic down before the Lord.

420
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:46,460
And so you can see just how much they wanted it,

421
00:21:46,460 --> 00:21:49,460
and how firmly they believed the Lord could help.

422
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:51,460
Today the Lord can help you too,

423
00:21:51,460 --> 00:21:53,460
no matter what situation you're in.

424
00:21:53,460 --> 00:21:55,460
The Lord saw their faith,

425
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:56,460
and said to the paralytic,

426
00:21:56,460 --> 00:21:59,460
He said, "Son, your sins are forgiven."

427
00:21:59,460 --> 00:22:00,460
What does "Son" mean here?

428
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:01,460
"Son" —

429
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:03,460
a young lad.

430
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:06,460
I find this quite meaningful.

431
00:22:06,460 --> 00:22:08,460
The Lord didn't merely forgive his sins.

432
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:13,460
You'll notice there's a warmth, a tenderness in the Lord.

433
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:16,220
saying, "Son, your sins are now forgiven."

434
00:22:16,220 --> 00:22:17,760
From this too you can see

435
00:22:17,760 --> 00:22:20,360
that some illnesses today,

436
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:23,560
and some troubles, are brought on by sin.

437
00:22:23,560 --> 00:22:30,060
Truly — for instance, why do some people struggle with mental illness?

438
00:22:30,060 --> 00:22:32,860
Because sometimes they harbor resentment,

439
00:22:32,860 --> 00:22:35,660
they're angry, unwilling to forgive,

440
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:38,560
dwelling on it, brooding day and night,

441
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,560
and it ends up like this.

442
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,060
Some keep turning over how others wronged them,

443
00:22:43,060 --> 00:22:46,900
some dwell on all kinds of lustful things,

444
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,720
and in the end it affects the body.

445
00:22:49,980 --> 00:22:51,500
So you see, sin

446
00:22:52,020 --> 00:22:52,780
can sometimes

447
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:54,320
cause a person

448
00:22:54,580 --> 00:22:55,340
to fall ill.

449
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:58,420
What did the Lord say? He said, "Your sins are forgiven."

450
00:22:59,180 --> 00:23:01,240
At the time, many people really were crowding around the Lord,

451
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:03,020
and there were some scribes,

452
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:05,840
scribes being those who copied out the Scriptures.

453
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:09,420
They knew the Scriptures and knew God,

454
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:10,460
to some degree.

455
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:12,760
But a few scribes were sitting there,

456
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:19,460
which shows they'd come early, or held some standing —

457
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:21,760
others couldn't even get in, yet they got to sit here.

458
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:26,620
In their hearts they were reasoning — not out loud — saying to themselves,

459
00:23:26,620 --> 00:23:29,960
Why does this man speak like this?

460
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:32,260
He is speaking blasphemy!

461
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:34,300
For apart from God,

462
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:36,620
who can forgive sins?

463
00:23:36,620 --> 00:23:37,900
What is blasphemy?

464
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:40,700
Blasphemy is presumptuous speech,

465
00:23:40,700 --> 00:23:41,980
speech that oversteps.

466
00:23:41,980 --> 00:23:46,980
If He cannot forgive sins and yet says "your sins are forgiven,"

467
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:49,980
that is overstepping — that is blasphemy.

468
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:54,980
So the passage explains it: apart from God, who can forgive sins?

469
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:58,980
Of course, only the One who executes judgment,

470
00:23:58,980 --> 00:24:02,980
who has the authority to condemn a person's sin,

471
00:24:02,980 --> 00:24:04,980
also has the authority to forgive a person's sin.

472
00:24:04,980 --> 00:24:08,980
They were reasoning in their hearts — perhaps just exchanging glances —

473
00:24:08,980 --> 00:24:10,980
but they said nothing aloud.

474
00:24:10,980 --> 00:24:12,300
But what does the Bible say?

475
00:24:12,300 --> 00:24:16,100
Jesus knew in His spirit that they were reasoning this way within themselves,

476
00:24:16,100 --> 00:24:17,560
and He said to them,

477
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:20,700
"Why do you reason these things in your hearts?

478
00:24:21,480 --> 00:24:23,660
Which is easier — to say to the paralytic, 'Your sins are forgiven,'

479
00:24:23,660 --> 00:24:26,580
or to say, 'Rise, take up your mat and walk'?

480
00:24:26,580 --> 00:24:30,720
Which of these two is easier to say?"

481
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:35,060
"But that you may know the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins" —

482
00:24:35,060 --> 00:24:37,320
then He said to the paralytic,

483
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:41,820
He said, "I tell you, rise, take up your mat, and go home."

484
00:24:41,820 --> 00:24:47,520
I think from this passage you can see several things.

485
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:49,200
First, who is the Lord Jesus?

486
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:52,900
He actually knew the thoughts within people's hearts.

487
00:24:52,900 --> 00:24:57,760
Perhaps they really were just glancing at one another,

488
00:24:57,760 --> 00:24:59,960
and the Lord saw their reaction —

489
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:01,740
the Lord's heart may simply be very perceptive.

490
00:25:01,740 --> 00:25:04,160
But what you see is this:

491
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:07,240
even the reasoning within their hearts —

492
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:08,520
the "why —

493
00:25:08,760 --> 00:25:11,840
why is your saying that this young man's sins are forgiven

494
00:25:12,100 --> 00:25:13,120
blasphemy?" —

495
00:25:13,380 --> 00:25:15,420
the Lord knew this doubt of theirs,

496
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:17,220
and the Lord put a question to them.

497
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:18,760
He said to them,

498
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:22,340
is it easier to forgive sins, or to say, "Rise, take up your mat and walk"?

499
00:25:23,360 --> 00:25:26,440
Let me ask you all: which of these two do you think is easier to say?

500
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:31,300
For people, for me,

501
00:25:32,060 --> 00:25:33,080
perhaps for all of you,

502
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:35,640
of course "your sins are forgiven" is the easier one.

503
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,400
Why is that?

504
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:38,200
After you say it, are the sins actually forgiven?

505
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:38,960
Who can tell?

506
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:42,300
You can't see it; nothing seems to happen.

507
00:25:42,800 --> 00:25:44,600
You just say it, and that's that.

508
00:25:44,860 --> 00:25:47,420
Some people say it and leave it at that.

509
00:25:47,680 --> 00:25:49,720
So "your sins are forgiven" seems the easier thing to say.

510
00:25:49,980 --> 00:25:52,800
But if you tell him to rise and take up his mat and walk,

511
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:56,380
and then the paralytic struggles for minutes and still can't get up,

512
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:57,920
well, that's trouble.

513
00:25:58,940 --> 00:25:59,960
Right away

514
00:26:00,480 --> 00:26:02,520
it tests whether your words are true.

515
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:07,640
So for people, "your sins are forgiven" might seem the easier thing,

516
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:11,220
but in the Lord's heart, in the Lord's eyes,

517
00:26:11,220 --> 00:26:14,800
forgiving a person's sin is actually the harder thing.

518
00:26:16,600 --> 00:26:17,360
It is harder.

519
00:26:17,620 --> 00:26:19,920
We'll explain a little later why it's harder.

520
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:25,040
But the Lord said: so that you may know —

521
00:26:25,300 --> 00:26:26,840
"the Son of Man" refers to the Lord Jesus —

522
00:26:27,100 --> 00:26:29,660
the Lord has authority on earth to forgive sins.

523
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:31,960
So the Lord said to the paralytic,

524
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:34,260
"Rise, take up your mat and walk."

525
00:26:34,780 --> 00:26:36,320
I think the Lord is truly so considerate.

526
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:38,880
He told him to get up,

527
00:26:39,120 --> 00:26:40,660
and the paralytic really did get up,

528
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:42,720
picked up his mat, and walked.

529
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:48,600
The Lord wasn't fussing over the mat — as if to say, you dropped this mat,

530
00:26:48,860 --> 00:26:52,440
it's dirty, take it with you, don't leave your trash behind.

531
00:26:53,460 --> 00:26:57,300
As I said, the mat was like a circumstance ruling over him; before, he was lame,

532
00:26:57,560 --> 00:27:01,400
couldn't walk — wherever the mat went, he went.

533
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:05,900
But today the Lord enabled him to walk; now he could carry the mat himself.

534
00:27:05,900 --> 00:27:10,700
No longer ruled by his circumstances, he could now handle them,

535
00:27:10,700 --> 00:27:14,700
he could deal with them. Those who believe in the Lord today are just like this.

536
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:17,500
It's not that nothing happens to us in our experience,

537
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:20,100
but rather that all kinds of things happen in life,

538
00:27:20,100 --> 00:27:23,200
and I'm able to handle them, able to deal with them.

539
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:25,300
The Lord gives us this ability.

540
00:27:25,300 --> 00:27:29,700
The man got up at once, took his mat, and walked.

541
00:27:29,700 --> 00:27:31,900
What did the people there record?

542
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:38,200
They were all amazed — astonished, taken aback.

543
00:27:38,200 --> 00:27:40,200
Seeing it, they gave glory to God. Why?

544
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:42,200
Because this was clearly a miracle.

545
00:27:42,200 --> 00:27:46,200
That is, if He had spoken blasphemy,

546
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:48,200
how could He then perform a miracle?

547
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:51,200
The Lord's clear performing of a miracle proves

548
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:53,200
that He truly had not spoken blasphemy.

549
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:54,700
He was not blaspheming God.

550
00:27:54,700 --> 00:27:56,200
And if that is so,

551
00:27:56,200 --> 00:27:59,520
then the Lord truly does have authority to forgive people's sins.

552
00:27:59,780 --> 00:28:01,320
So those people were amazed:

553
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:03,880
"We have never seen anything like this!"

554
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:08,240
They had truly never once seen such a thing before —

555
00:28:08,480 --> 00:28:10,280
and it's not that they had never seen

556
00:28:10,540 --> 00:28:11,300
a lame man before

557
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:13,100
get healed and be made to walk again.

558
00:28:13,600 --> 00:28:14,380
After all,

559
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:17,700
the Lord had already performed miracles and healed a great many people before this.

560
00:28:18,220 --> 00:28:19,500
At the very least, those four friends themselves

561
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:21,040
had this very kind of faith,

562
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:25,380
believing that bringing the paralytic right before the Lord would surely bring him healing and help.

563
00:28:25,380 --> 00:28:29,300
So when they say, "We have never once seen anything like this,"

564
00:28:29,300 --> 00:28:32,860
it doesn't merely mean a lame man getting up and walking,

565
00:28:32,860 --> 00:28:35,260
but rather that here on this earth,

566
00:28:35,260 --> 00:28:42,660
God could actually grant to a man the very authority to forgive people's sins.

567
00:28:42,660 --> 00:28:43,780
And by their very own words they had said,

568
00:28:43,780 --> 00:28:46,380
apart from God alone, who else can possibly forgive sins?

569
00:28:46,380 --> 00:28:49,300
But the Lord had clearly and plainly performed a miracle,

570
00:28:49,300 --> 00:28:51,500
and this proved that He truly is able to forgive sins.

571
00:28:51,500 --> 00:28:54,180
And that means the One standing right there before their very eyes was —

572
00:28:54,180 --> 00:28:56,180
none other than the Son of God, God Himself.

573
00:28:58,660 --> 00:28:59,780
Now do you understand this?

574
00:29:04,320 --> 00:29:07,120
The Bible tells us that God is not only love,

575
00:29:07,580 --> 00:29:08,620
longing so deeply for people to receive

576
00:29:09,020 --> 00:29:10,220
all of His goodness,

577
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:11,580
and all of His riches,

578
00:29:11,820 --> 00:29:12,480
and all of His love.

579
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:14,780
The Bible also tells us plainly that God is light,

580
00:29:15,220 --> 00:29:16,920
and wherever there is light, there can be no darkness at all.

581
00:29:19,980 --> 00:29:22,880
Now you just said that God is so real, and that He is so good —

582
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:25,880
so then why is it that I can't feel Him, why can't I experience Him for myself?

583
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:29,880
Well, this picture here explains the whole situation.

584
00:29:29,880 --> 00:29:32,880
God is still light, and He is still love,

585
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:36,880
but today so many people are completely cut off from God,

586
00:29:36,880 --> 00:29:38,880
and what exactly is this wall between them?

587
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:41,880
It is nothing other than the sin that they have committed.

588
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:47,880
The Bible says that it is our sins that have separated us from God.

589
00:29:47,880 --> 00:29:50,346
This very thick wall here,

590
00:29:50,346 --> 00:29:52,072
this great wall of sin,

591
00:29:52,072 --> 00:29:54,291
has walled us right off from God —

592
00:29:54,291 --> 00:29:55,770
and it has not merely separated us,

593
00:29:55,770 --> 00:29:57,250
but has cut us off from Him completely,

594
00:29:57,250 --> 00:29:59,716
so that we can no longer see God at all,

595
00:29:59,716 --> 00:30:01,195
can no longer feel Him,

596
00:30:01,195 --> 00:30:02,675
and can no longer experience Him,

597
00:30:02,675 --> 00:30:04,894
and we ourselves are left in great pain because of it.

598
00:30:04,894 --> 00:30:05,880
And why is that?

599
00:30:05,880 --> 00:30:08,880
Because once we are cut off from the God of light and holiness,

600
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:12,820
life is left without any hope, and is lived out down in the shadows,

601
00:30:12,820 --> 00:30:14,320
still carrying about the burden of sin,

602
00:30:14,320 --> 00:30:15,920
and weighed right down by its heavy load.

603
00:30:15,920 --> 00:30:17,700
You see this man here,

604
00:30:17,700 --> 00:30:19,500
all bound up by a heavy chain.

605
00:30:19,500 --> 00:30:21,240
Now if you were to ask a great many people,

606
00:30:21,240 --> 00:30:22,420
do you really want to be good?

607
00:30:22,420 --> 00:30:24,260
Do you want to stop cursing and swearing?

608
00:30:24,260 --> 00:30:25,920
Do you want to stop telling lies?

609
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:28,580
Do you want to stop flying into a temper?

610
00:30:28,580 --> 00:30:30,020
A great many people will tell you,

611
00:30:30,020 --> 00:30:30,640
why, of course I do.

612
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:32,920
After all, who really wants to be bad?

613
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:34,560
But here is the real problem,

614
00:30:34,560 --> 00:30:39,560
once a person has sinned, he becomes a slave to that sin, and he simply cannot overcome it.

615
00:30:39,560 --> 00:30:45,560
There was once a man who used to curse, and he tried his very hardest —

616
00:30:45,560 --> 00:30:50,560
he made a New Year's resolution to stop his cursing; one day was fine, two days were fine,

617
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:55,560
but before even a week was out he was right back at it again, and even worse than he was before.

618
00:30:55,560 --> 00:30:59,560
So you see, to sin is to become a slave to sin.

619
00:30:59,560 --> 00:31:03,920
And not only that — there are real consequences as well: sin brings about death,

620
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:07,760
and even after death, there still remains the judgment.

621
00:31:07,760 --> 00:31:14,160
Now you might well say, but I've never murdered anyone or set any fires,

622
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:16,720
I've committed no crime at all, and I have no criminal record,

623
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:20,800
I even hold a certificate of good conduct — that's the very reason I was able to immigrate here to New Zealand.

624
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:25,420
Murder, arson, rape, and pillage — all of those things, of course, are sins.

625
00:31:25,420 --> 00:31:27,980
But what is it that the Bible actually says sin is?

626
00:31:27,980 --> 00:31:31,300
It says that anything at all which goes against the conscience is sin.

627
00:31:31,560 --> 00:31:32,340
Now it's a very curious thing.

628
00:31:33,100 --> 00:31:36,420
Today may well be the very first time that I've ever met you,

629
00:31:36,940 --> 00:31:37,960
and yet deep in your own heart,

630
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:40,780
you already know that what I'm telling you is true.

631
00:31:41,540 --> 00:31:42,820
You see, you have a conscience within you.

632
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:44,880
You already know what is right and what is wrong,

633
00:31:45,380 --> 00:31:47,180
and these aren't things that you ever learned out of any book.

634
00:31:47,700 --> 00:31:49,480
You don't need to raise up your hand

635
00:31:50,260 --> 00:31:53,320
and ask, "Teacher, is it wrong to cheat on the exam?" You don't need to ask at all — you already know in yourself.

636
00:31:53,840 --> 00:31:55,620
And you won't go and ask your own mother,

637
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:57,160
"Mother, is it wrong for me to steal your money?"

638
00:31:57,160 --> 00:32:05,160
People simply have a conscience, and anything that goes against that conscience is sin.

639
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:13,160
Now some will say, well, I'm just a bit petty about things, or I dwell on a few lustful thoughts now and then,

640
00:32:13,160 --> 00:32:16,160
but I never once acted on it, and I never hurt anybody.

641
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:21,160
But one of the truly terrible things about sin is that you can never take it back again.

642
00:32:21,160 --> 00:32:25,160
Take that friend I mentioned earlier, the one who cursed —

643
00:32:25,160 --> 00:32:28,410
cursing away while chatting with others came very easily to him,

644
00:32:28,410 --> 00:32:31,910
but then on one occasion he got himself into a fight,

645
00:32:31,910 --> 00:32:36,160
and the whole reason for that fight was that the other man had cursed at him first.

646
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:42,160
So you see, one of the truly terrifying things about the sinful mindset is just this: you simply cannot reverse it.

647
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:46,518
For instance, take a man who dwells on lustful things.

648
00:32:46,518 --> 00:32:49,291
Take some husbands, for example —

649
00:32:49,291 --> 00:32:51,272
as the old saying goes, "a man who isn't a bit of a playboy

650
00:32:51,272 --> 00:32:52,460
in his youth

651
00:32:52,460 --> 00:32:58,560
has wasted his youth," and so he takes one mistress after another. But if his wife were to turn and say to him,

652
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:03,560
well, how would you like it if I went and had myself a lover, and then a second one, and even a third?

653
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:11,060
You'd find he would flare right up in anger. So you see, the real terror of sin is that he cannot turn it around again,

654
00:33:11,060 --> 00:33:15,740
along with that whole mindset — that deeply self-centered mindset.

655
00:33:15,740 --> 00:33:19,740
So that is why, in English, sin is actually called "sin."

656
00:33:19,740 --> 00:33:24,940
The S is for "selfish," the I right there in the very center — the self placed at the center — and the N, for nothing else at all.

657
00:33:24,940 --> 00:33:32,060
And God is light, and He utterly hates all sin.

658
00:33:32,060 --> 00:33:35,652
Now we were just speaking a moment ago about sin —

659
00:33:35,652 --> 00:33:41,040
and besides separating a person right off from God,

660
00:33:41,040 --> 00:33:42,840
and leaving him thoroughly unhappy,

661
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:44,360
it truly does leave a person's whole life

662
00:33:44,620 --> 00:33:46,420
completely without hope.

663
00:33:46,680 --> 00:33:48,200
with no way out at all. Now I recently saw a news story.

664
00:33:48,980 --> 00:33:50,000
And what was it that this story was about?

665
00:33:50,260 --> 00:33:52,300
Over in Switzerland they had invented a so-called

666
00:33:52,820 --> 00:33:53,580
machine designed to help people

667
00:33:53,840 --> 00:33:55,880
end their own lives — a euthanasia machine.

668
00:33:56,400 --> 00:33:57,940
Now you would find a thing like that very strange indeed.

669
00:33:58,960 --> 00:34:03,060
Why would people ever take their own lives — apart, of course, from those with some terminal illness?

670
00:34:03,320 --> 00:34:04,840
Some people, perhaps, simply

671
00:34:05,100 --> 00:34:06,380
feel that there is nothing left for them to live for anymore.

672
00:34:06,900 --> 00:34:08,680
You lie yourself down inside of it,

673
00:34:08,680 --> 00:34:11,400
and very soon nitrogen gas is released, and you lose consciousness,

674
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:12,360
and then after that, you die.

675
00:34:12,360 --> 00:34:13,760
You might well find the whole thing very strange —

676
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:14,900
why, of all the things in the world to go and invent,

677
00:34:14,900 --> 00:34:16,500
would anyone ever invent a machine for committing suicide?

678
00:34:16,500 --> 00:34:18,620
From this too you can clearly see

679
00:34:18,620 --> 00:34:21,400
the deep hopelessness that people feel inside,

680
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:23,680
once they have been cut off from God —

681
00:34:23,680 --> 00:34:26,480
that terrible darkness with no way out of it at all.

682
00:34:26,480 --> 00:34:32,400
Earlier on, back while we were leading the hymn,

683
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:33,620
I had mentioned this particular verse.

684
00:34:33,620 --> 00:34:35,260
It says: it is appointed

685
00:34:35,260 --> 00:34:37,080
for everyone to die once,

686
00:34:37,080 --> 00:34:40,280
and after death, the judgment. God is perfectly just.

687
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:44,380
So the poor will die, but the rich will die too.

688
00:34:44,380 --> 00:34:46,280
Those with millions will die.

689
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:50,840
The powerless and oppressed will die,

690
00:34:50,840 --> 00:34:54,580
but the oppressors, the dictators, will die just the same.

691
00:34:54,580 --> 00:34:58,640
Everyone dies once, but death is not the end of it.

692
00:34:58,640 --> 00:35:03,360
Each will be judged according to what he did in his life.

693
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:06,160
The wages of sin is death,

694
00:35:06,160 --> 00:35:10,000
and all who sin are cast into hell.

695
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:11,800
Hell is a

696
00:35:12,040 --> 00:35:12,820
lake of fire,

697
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:14,860
a lake of fire that is never quenched.

698
00:35:15,640 --> 00:35:17,160
There was a recent news story:

699
00:35:17,680 --> 00:35:18,200
someone

700
00:35:18,440 --> 00:35:20,240
took three hundred thousand photographs

701
00:35:20,500 --> 00:35:22,540
and assembled them into a single image — this one.

702
00:35:23,320 --> 00:35:26,900
It's been called the clearest picture of the sun ever taken.

703
00:35:27,660 --> 00:35:29,200
Three hundred thousand photos pieced together.

704
00:35:29,960 --> 00:35:32,020
You see this ball of fire,

705
00:35:33,040 --> 00:35:34,060
burning for billions of years.

706
00:35:36,160 --> 00:35:39,428
If God can make a sun

707
00:35:39,428 --> 00:35:41,210
that burns for so long,

708
00:35:41,210 --> 00:35:45,964
then you can be sure God will, for all who sin,

709
00:35:45,964 --> 00:35:48,043
prepare a place —

710
00:35:48,043 --> 00:35:48,935
hell,

711
00:35:48,935 --> 00:35:50,420
a lake of fire.

712
00:35:51,160 --> 00:35:52,664
In fact, in the Bible,

713
00:35:52,664 --> 00:35:54,356
the One who spoke most about hell is the Lord Himself.

714
00:35:54,356 --> 00:35:56,236
He said, if your eye causes you to sin,

715
00:35:56,236 --> 00:35:57,928
pluck it out;

716
00:35:57,928 --> 00:35:59,432
it is better to enter paradise with one eye

717
00:35:59,432 --> 00:36:01,500
than with both eyes to be thrown into hell.

718
00:36:01,500 --> 00:36:08,920
If your hand causes you to sin, cut it off; better to enter paradise without a hand than with both hands to go to hell.

719
00:36:08,920 --> 00:36:11,740
But He doesn't mean you should actually pluck out your eye or cut off your hand — no.

720
00:36:11,740 --> 00:36:16,600
He means: whatever the cost, do not go to hell.

721
00:36:16,600 --> 00:36:18,284
The Lord loves you dearly,

722
00:36:18,284 --> 00:36:19,406
He loves people,

723
00:36:19,406 --> 00:36:20,810
and He is saying,

724
00:36:20,810 --> 00:36:23,616
don't come to such an end,

725
00:36:23,616 --> 00:36:25,300
don't go to hell.

726
00:36:25,300 --> 00:36:32,140
So God sent His beloved Son, the Lord Jesus, into the world,

727
00:36:32,140 --> 00:36:33,500
and most importantly —

728
00:36:33,500 --> 00:36:35,960
yes, He healed many people's diseases,

729
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:37,500
comforted many broken hearts,

730
00:36:37,500 --> 00:36:39,980
changed many lives —

731
00:36:39,980 --> 00:36:41,960
but the most important thing of all

732
00:36:41,960 --> 00:36:43,840
is that, for our sins,

733
00:36:43,840 --> 00:36:46,600
He bore the punishment.

734
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:48,800
God is just.

735
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:50,820
He will by no means clear the guilty.

736
00:36:50,820 --> 00:36:53,620
If a judge found you guilty,

737
00:36:53,620 --> 00:36:56,620
and said, "I love you, so I declare you innocent,"

738
00:36:56,620 --> 00:36:59,120
then something is wrong with that judge.

739
00:36:59,120 --> 00:37:01,620
That judge himself is at fault, that judge himself is unjust,

740
00:37:01,620 --> 00:37:05,120
because he's covering for you, isn't he?

741
00:37:05,120 --> 00:37:07,620
So when God would forgive us,

742
00:37:07,620 --> 00:37:11,620
He had to do it in a way that was just.

743
00:37:11,620 --> 00:37:14,120
That's why, with the paralytic we spoke of,

744
00:37:14,120 --> 00:37:16,120
when the Lord said, "Your sins are forgiven,"

745
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:18,120
it was in fact a very hard thing to say.

746
00:37:18,120 --> 00:37:22,620
Yet from the very start the Lord spoke to him the hardest words,

747
00:37:22,620 --> 00:37:24,300
declaring that He was willing.

748
00:37:24,300 --> 00:37:26,300
When He said He forgave that man's sin,

749
00:37:26,300 --> 00:37:27,580
perhaps He already had in mind

750
00:37:27,580 --> 00:37:29,620
that one day, for him —

751
00:37:29,620 --> 00:37:32,300
for the sins of mankind — He would pay the price.

752
00:37:32,300 --> 00:37:34,100
But the Lord Jesus' greatest,

753
00:37:34,100 --> 00:37:35,500
most important act was this:

754
00:37:35,500 --> 00:37:37,860
to bear the punishment for our sins,

755
00:37:37,860 --> 00:37:39,220
hanging upon the tree.

756
00:37:39,220 --> 00:37:40,260
So this is why the Bible says

757
00:37:40,260 --> 00:37:41,740
that He loved me

758
00:37:41,740 --> 00:37:43,300
and that He gave His very own self up for me.

759
00:37:47,740 --> 00:37:50,180
Now in the Lord Jesus' final days on earth,

760
00:37:50,180 --> 00:37:54,180
He had done so many miracles and so very much good,

761
00:37:54,180 --> 00:37:58,180
and yet, out of sheer hatred and jealousy, the people came to hate Him,

762
00:37:58,180 --> 00:38:01,180
hating Him entirely without cause, and seeking to destroy Him.

763
00:38:01,180 --> 00:38:05,180
They used a great many false witnesses in order to frame the Lord,

764
00:38:05,180 --> 00:38:07,180
speaking all manner of lies against Him,

765
00:38:07,180 --> 00:38:10,180
claiming that He had said things which He had never once said,

766
00:38:10,180 --> 00:38:13,180
all in order to force His crucifixion.

767
00:38:13,180 --> 00:38:16,180
Now crucifixion was a most cruel and terrible punishment.

768
00:38:16,180 --> 00:38:23,680
Before He was ever nailed to the cross, they wove together a crown of thorns and pressed it down onto the Lord's head,

769
00:38:23,680 --> 00:38:28,680
and they draped a purple robe over Him, all the while mocking Him and jeering at Him.

770
00:38:28,680 --> 00:38:35,680
As we said earlier, "Bethlehem Ephrathah — out of you shall come forth a ruler" —

771
00:38:35,680 --> 00:38:39,680
So you're the king, are you? You're the one who's going to rule? Congratulations to you, they sneered at Him.

772
00:38:39,680 --> 00:38:45,680
So they crowned Him with those thorns, and robed Him in that purple, and they mocked Him,

773
00:38:45,680 --> 00:38:51,680
and they struck Him with their hands, and spat right into His face — oh, a terrible humiliation.

774
00:38:51,680 --> 00:38:53,680
And what is it that the Bible says about this?

775
00:38:53,680 --> 00:38:59,680
Yet the Lord set His face like a flint, for He was fully determined to go through all of this for our sake.

776
00:38:59,680 --> 00:39:06,680
Three nails fixed Him fast to the cross; and even before that, they had scourged the Lord.

777
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:11,680
The whip they used was a cat-o'-nine-tails — a single whip splitting out into nine separate tails.

778
00:39:11,680 --> 00:39:13,680
An ordinary whip lands with a crack,

779
00:39:13,680 --> 00:39:17,680
but this one had bits of metal on the ends,

780
00:39:17,680 --> 00:39:21,680
sinking into the flesh and tearing it out in a bloody mess.

781
00:39:21,680 --> 00:39:23,680
The Bible says the Lord's back

782
00:39:23,680 --> 00:39:25,680
was like a field plowed by oxen,

783
00:39:25,680 --> 00:39:29,680
its furrows deep and long.

784
00:39:29,680 --> 00:39:32,680
There are records of this:

785
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:35,680
some people died from the scourging alone,

786
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:37,680
because even their inner organs were exposed.

787
00:39:37,680 --> 00:39:40,680
There's not much flesh on the back.

788
00:39:40,680 --> 00:39:43,520
They beat the Lord terribly.

789
00:39:43,680 --> 00:39:47,920
Why does it dwell on how severely He was beaten?

790
00:39:47,920 --> 00:39:51,400
Because the governor at the time, Pilate,

791
00:39:51,400 --> 00:39:53,880
wanted to use this to win the crowd's sympathy.

792
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:55,540
He said to them,

793
00:39:55,540 --> 00:39:58,400
I find no fault in this Jesus,

794
00:39:58,400 --> 00:39:59,800
yet he had Him scourged,

795
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:03,320
tormented until He hardly looked human,

796
00:40:03,320 --> 00:40:04,900
then brought the Lord Jesus out

797
00:40:04,900 --> 00:40:05,540
and said to them,

798
00:40:05,540 --> 00:40:06,880
Behold the man!

799
00:40:06,880 --> 00:40:10,220
He's already been beaten so severely.

800
00:40:10,220 --> 00:40:12,680
His aim was to stir the crowd's sympathy.

801
00:40:12,680 --> 00:40:14,720
I find not the slightest guilt in Him,

802
00:40:14,980 --> 00:40:17,040
I know it's out of envy that you handed Him over,

803
00:40:17,280 --> 00:40:20,100
and I've already had Him beaten like this — it should be enough.

804
00:40:20,620 --> 00:40:22,400
But those people were set on rejecting the Lord.

805
00:40:22,660 --> 00:40:23,680
They would not have Him.

806
00:40:23,940 --> 00:40:25,480
They demanded He be crucified.

807
00:40:26,240 --> 00:40:29,320
So with three nails, a man of over a hundred pounds was hung

808
00:40:29,840 --> 00:40:30,600
upon the wood.

809
00:40:34,960 --> 00:40:35,460
In fact —

810
00:40:35,980 --> 00:40:37,260
just imagine —

811
00:40:38,280 --> 00:40:39,040
He is the true God,

812
00:40:39,300 --> 00:40:42,640
the One who made heaven and earth; yet the Maker of heaven and earth, in this world,

813
00:40:42,680 --> 00:40:44,980
could not find a single place to stand,

814
00:40:45,760 --> 00:40:48,320
hung between heaven and earth, reaching neither.

815
00:40:50,360 --> 00:40:51,900
Rejected to such a degree.

816
00:40:53,940 --> 00:40:57,280
But there's meaning in it too — hanging there between heaven and earth,

817
00:40:57,520 --> 00:40:58,560
so that today we

818
00:40:58,800 --> 00:41:01,360
might have a living way back to God.

819
00:41:01,620 --> 00:41:03,160
He became a ladder to heaven.

820
00:41:04,440 --> 00:41:07,000
Three nails held up a man of over a hundred pounds.

821
00:41:07,260 --> 00:41:10,080
Naturally it was agony, the blood flowing without stop.

822
00:41:10,080 --> 00:41:13,760
And when you're hung up like that, you cannot breathe.

823
00:41:13,760 --> 00:41:15,540
Your weight pulls you forward,

824
00:41:15,540 --> 00:41:16,460
and you can't draw breath.

825
00:41:16,460 --> 00:41:19,680
So each time you breathe, you have to push yourself up and back,

826
00:41:19,680 --> 00:41:22,420
but your back has been flayed open.

827
00:41:22,420 --> 00:41:24,180
Each time you press back,

828
00:41:24,180 --> 00:41:25,960
your raw back

829
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:30,100
scrapes against the splintered wood,

830
00:41:30,100 --> 00:41:31,840
so every single breath is agony.

831
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:33,860
With every movement,

832
00:41:33,860 --> 00:41:36,040
the wounds where the nails pierced

833
00:41:36,040 --> 00:41:37,440
tear wider and longer,

834
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:38,420
wider and longer.

835
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:45,080
He hung on the cross for six hours, from nine in the morning until three in the afternoon.

836
00:41:47,080 --> 00:41:50,080
And at noon, the sky turned dark.

837
00:41:51,080 --> 00:41:56,080
We spoke of that ball of fire, the sun, burning so long —

838
00:41:56,080 --> 00:42:00,080
yet at midday, from twelve noon until three in the afternoon,

839
00:42:00,080 --> 00:42:06,080
the Bible says darkness came over all the land. Why?

840
00:42:06,080 --> 00:42:14,080
I find it striking: this was the darkest hour in the universe — the One who least deserved to die, dying;

841
00:42:14,080 --> 00:42:19,080
the One without sin, hung upon the tree for us.

842
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:25,080
This was no solar eclipse, for an eclipse never lasts three hours,

843
00:42:25,080 --> 00:42:29,080
and besides, if you know that day was the fourteenth of the month,

844
00:42:29,080 --> 00:42:35,080
the moon was not between the sun and the earth; the moon was far off,

845
00:42:35,080 --> 00:42:38,920
with the earth in between — so it was no eclipse.

846
00:42:39,940 --> 00:42:42,000
Now if you were to ask me why it was that the whole land went dark,

847
00:42:42,500 --> 00:42:45,320
whether the sun itself withheld its light for a time —

848
00:42:45,580 --> 00:42:46,860
well, I honestly don't know the reason for it.

849
00:42:47,620 --> 00:42:51,980
But it does seem to be saying something to us: that God wanted all people to take careful note of one thing.

850
00:42:52,740 --> 00:42:54,800
It's just like on a stage, when all the lights suddenly go out

851
00:42:55,300 --> 00:42:58,640
and a single spotlight comes to fall right on the center, right upon the Lord —

852
00:42:58,880 --> 00:43:00,160
everyone there simply must pay close attention to this.

853
00:43:00,420 --> 00:43:01,700
As all of heaven and earth went dark,

854
00:43:01,700 --> 00:43:04,400
every last person ought to take careful note of this one thing:

855
00:43:04,400 --> 00:43:05,560
that the Son of God Himself,

856
00:43:05,560 --> 00:43:08,220
hung there upon the tree for us,

857
00:43:08,220 --> 00:43:11,180
and became a curse on our behalf,

858
00:43:11,180 --> 00:43:13,720
bearing the full weight of our sins.

859
00:43:13,720 --> 00:43:18,920
And so at this very point,

860
00:43:18,920 --> 00:43:22,400
I would very much love to share a hymn together with you.

861
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:24,820
This particular hymn is called

862
00:43:24,820 --> 00:43:25,780
"Come,

863
00:43:25,780 --> 00:43:27,420
Come and Feel."

864
00:43:27,420 --> 00:43:31,200
And I do hope that you will take in the Lord's great love for you,

865
00:43:31,200 --> 00:43:36,200
and His whole heart toward you — just where His love for you truly lies.

866
00:43:36,200 --> 00:43:39,200
He was so willing to pass through every last suffering and every hardship for us.

867
00:44:01,200 --> 00:44:08,140
God's love is displayed upon the cross;

868
00:44:08,140 --> 00:44:15,240
for me the Lord endured torment and scorn,

869
00:44:15,240 --> 00:44:21,900
shamed by men,

870
00:44:21,900 --> 00:44:26,800
heaped with slander.

871
00:44:26,800 --> 00:44:31,300
The Father's beloved Son tasted

872
00:44:31,300 --> 00:44:35,800
every mockery and torment,

873
00:44:35,800 --> 00:44:40,244
crowned with thorns,

874
00:44:40,244 --> 00:44:45,800
and cruelly scourged,

875
00:44:45,800 --> 00:44:54,800
His body covered over with wounds.

876
00:44:54,800 --> 00:44:59,244
Hands and feet nailed fast,

877
00:44:59,244 --> 00:45:04,800
hung high upon the wood,

878
00:45:04,800 --> 00:45:08,800
in utter agony —

879
00:45:08,800 --> 00:45:13,800
who can feel it?

880
00:45:24,800 --> 00:45:54,780
The pain that never ceases.

881
00:45:54,780 --> 00:46:00,040
His face gaunt and wasted,

882
00:46:00,040 --> 00:46:07,040
hung on the cross, His bones now all laid bare,

883
00:46:07,040 --> 00:46:14,400
blood streaming down His face,

884
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:19,040
dripping to the ground,

885
00:46:19,040 --> 00:46:21,400
sorely wounded,

886
00:46:21,400 --> 00:46:28,200
yet struck even by the Father.

887
00:46:28,200 --> 00:46:32,467
Who could write a poem

888
00:46:32,467 --> 00:46:37,800
to capture such love?

889
00:46:37,800 --> 00:46:41,978
His love,

890
00:46:41,978 --> 00:46:47,200
engraved within my heart.

891
00:46:47,200 --> 00:46:51,422
How fresh His mercy,

892
00:46:51,422 --> 00:46:56,700
deep and wide —

893
00:46:56,700 --> 00:47:00,700
the grace of the cross,

894
00:47:00,700 --> 00:47:05,700
who can ever fathom it?

895
00:47:05,700 --> 00:47:09,700
My Lord even

896
00:47:09,700 --> 00:47:14,700
cried out, "It is finished."

897
00:47:14,700 --> 00:47:23,700
I will ponder it ten thousand times over.

898
00:47:23,700 --> 00:47:28,144
Jesus, my Lord,

899
00:47:28,144 --> 00:47:33,700
Your love runs deep and will never die.

900
00:47:33,700 --> 00:47:37,700
This grace

901
00:47:37,700 --> 00:47:42,700
forever moves us.

902
00:47:42,700 --> 00:47:53,580
This deep grace — come, and feel it.

903
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:25,000
He loved me and gave Himself for me. (Galatians 2:20)

904
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:38,000
As the hymn just mentioned, there on the cross, at the very end, the Lord cried out aloud: "It is finished."

905
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:42,680
He had carried this one single purpose all along:

906
00:48:42,700 --> 00:48:43,980
to deal fully with our sins,

907
00:48:46,020 --> 00:48:47,300
and to bear our sins Himself,

908
00:48:51,140 --> 00:48:51,920
so that

909
00:48:52,180 --> 00:48:53,700
today our sins might truly be forgiven.

910
00:48:54,220 --> 00:48:55,760
He cried out, "It is finished."

911
00:48:56,260 --> 00:48:58,580
He had fully accomplished this great salvation.

912
00:49:01,640 --> 00:49:02,920
And so it turns out that God,

913
00:49:03,940 --> 00:49:05,220
in just exactly this way,

914
00:49:06,500 --> 00:49:07,540
had set out to save us all.

915
00:49:08,040 --> 00:49:10,340
The Bible says we, like sheep, have gone astray,

916
00:49:11,120 --> 00:49:12,660
each one of us turning to his own way,

917
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:19,360
and God the Father laid on the Lord Jesus the iniquity of us all.

918
00:49:19,360 --> 00:49:25,500
God used this very method of substitution in order to save you and me,

919
00:49:25,500 --> 00:49:29,080
crushing His own beloved Son in our place,

920
00:49:29,080 --> 00:49:32,240
and making Him our sin-bearing Lamb.

921
00:49:32,240 --> 00:49:34,980
So the Lord Jesus is indeed the Lamb of God,

922
00:49:34,980 --> 00:49:38,480
the holy One, utterly without any blemish,

923
00:49:38,480 --> 00:49:41,880
and yet He hung there on the cross for our sake.

924
00:49:41,880 --> 00:49:47,880
You know, the Chinese character for "righteousness," if you go and look it up, actually falls under the "sheep" radical.

925
00:49:47,880 --> 00:49:50,880
A lamb standing there in my place — that is the very picture of righteousness.

926
00:49:50,880 --> 00:49:54,880
So that today we are not only set free from sin, but are actually counted as righteous before God.

927
00:49:54,880 --> 00:49:58,880
The Lord died there in our place, and in doing so He brought us this precious gift,

928
00:49:58,880 --> 00:50:03,880
changing our very lives, and teaching us what is truly lovely and what is good.

929
00:50:03,880 --> 00:50:09,640
How precious it is — that the Lord did all of this for us;

930
00:50:09,640 --> 00:50:11,100
and then, on the third day after His death,

931
00:50:11,100 --> 00:50:13,280
He rose again from the dead.

932
00:50:13,280 --> 00:50:15,740
God raised the Lord up from the dead.

933
00:50:15,740 --> 00:50:18,020
The Lord Jesus rose again from among the dead,

934
00:50:18,020 --> 00:50:19,340
and this one thing declares to us plainly:

935
00:50:19,340 --> 00:50:21,320
that this salvation has now been fully accomplished.

936
00:50:21,320 --> 00:50:23,920
For if the Lord Himself had had any sin

937
00:50:23,920 --> 00:50:26,380
and had died on account of it,

938
00:50:26,380 --> 00:50:27,740
then He could never possibly have risen again.

939
00:50:27,740 --> 00:50:29,940
But the Lord's resurrection from the dead

940
00:50:29,940 --> 00:50:32,340
declares to us that He truly bore our sins,

941
00:50:32,340 --> 00:50:34,700
and that God Himself accepted this whole work of salvation.

942
00:50:34,700 --> 00:50:37,140
God raised the Lord up from death,

943
00:50:37,140 --> 00:50:38,900
and exalted Him with His own right hand,

944
00:50:38,900 --> 00:50:41,900
and gave to Him the name that is above every other name.

945
00:50:41,900 --> 00:50:44,360
And today this same risen Lord

946
00:50:44,360 --> 00:50:46,620
is able to help us walk the whole road of life,

947
00:50:46,620 --> 00:50:48,500
and He is able to be right there with us,

948
00:50:48,500 --> 00:50:49,980
so that my life is no longer lonely at all,

949
00:50:49,980 --> 00:50:51,880
and no longer like duckweed drifting aimlessly about.

950
00:50:51,880 --> 00:50:55,080
He hears every single one of our prayers,

951
00:50:55,080 --> 00:50:59,200
and He is able to teach us, to guide us, and to change our very lives,

952
00:50:59,200 --> 00:51:06,200
and to bring us all the way home — home to heaven, back before the Father Himself.

953
00:51:08,200 --> 00:51:14,200
So very many people, coming to know this salvation, have received the Lord as their Savior,

954
00:51:15,200 --> 00:51:18,200
and their lives have been changed, and their sins have been forgiven.

955
00:51:18,200 --> 00:51:20,200
So how is it that you believe in the Lord?

956
00:51:20,200 --> 00:51:25,200
Well, there's no paperwork at all to file; you need only to pray to the Lord sincerely.

957
00:51:25,200 --> 00:51:28,200
Lord, today I am willing to repent, and to sin no more.

958
00:51:29,200 --> 00:51:31,500
Please forgive all the sins of my whole life,

959
00:51:31,500 --> 00:51:34,580
and I am willing to receive You as my own Savior.

960
00:51:34,580 --> 00:51:35,860
It really is as simple as that.

961
00:51:35,860 --> 00:51:39,440
The Lord is so very glad indeed to hear your prayer,

962
00:51:39,440 --> 00:51:40,980
and glad to save you,

963
00:51:40,980 --> 00:51:42,760
and glad to be your very own Savior,

964
00:51:42,760 --> 00:51:45,580
and glad to walk the road of life right alongside you,

965
00:51:45,580 --> 00:51:50,200
and glad to change both your life now and your whole eternity,

966
00:51:50,200 --> 00:51:51,980
so that all those who believe in the Lord

967
00:51:51,980 --> 00:51:54,800
have their lives truly changed for good,

968
00:51:54,800 --> 00:51:56,600
and all their sins forgiven,

969
00:51:56,600 --> 00:51:59,160
and are fully reconciled to God,

970
00:51:59,160 --> 00:52:01,200
and become the very children of God,

971
00:52:01,200 --> 00:52:03,000
with an abundant and overflowing life.

972
00:52:03,000 --> 00:52:05,040
He said He came that people might have life,

973
00:52:05,040 --> 00:52:07,600
and have it more abundantly —

974
00:52:07,600 --> 00:52:09,660
to enjoy real and true love,

975
00:52:09,660 --> 00:52:10,940
and real peace and joy,

976
00:52:10,940 --> 00:52:13,240
and a living hope well worth boasting in:

977
00:52:13,240 --> 00:52:17,080
namely, that we have a bright and warm home waiting for us in heaven.

978
00:52:17,080 --> 00:52:19,380
So do you long to receive all of this grace for yourself?

979
00:52:19,380 --> 00:52:23,220
This is the very thing that God has prepared for you,

980
00:52:23,220 --> 00:52:25,020
and what God so dearly wants to give to you.

981
00:52:25,020 --> 00:52:28,340
Now why exactly is this called the "gospel" — the good news?

982
00:52:28,340 --> 00:52:32,940
Well, it's because He is so willing to deal fully with all our sins,

983
00:52:32,940 --> 00:52:38,580
and because He wants us to receive the very greatest and fullest happiness of all.

984
00:52:38,580 --> 00:52:42,160
So at this point I'd like to give you all just a moment,

985
00:52:42,160 --> 00:52:43,960
to be quite still, and to think.

986
00:52:43,960 --> 00:52:48,060
If there are any here among us who have not yet believed,

987
00:52:48,060 --> 00:52:51,120
who have not yet received the Lord Jesus as their Savior,

988
00:52:51,120 --> 00:52:56,760
I do hope that in this very moment you will go ahead and make this decision,

989
00:52:56,760 --> 00:52:59,320
to receive the Lord as your own Savior.

990
00:52:59,320 --> 00:53:03,420
You can experience for yourself the Lord changing your whole life,

991
00:53:03,420 --> 00:53:05,720
so that you are no longer down in the darkness at all,

992
00:53:05,720 --> 00:53:07,260
but can enter right into the light —

993
00:53:07,260 --> 00:53:09,820
and into a truly marvelous light at that.

994
00:53:09,820 --> 00:53:12,640
Believing in the Lord is a good thing indeed.

995
00:53:12,640 --> 00:53:13,660
So please don't hesitate about it.

996
00:53:13,660 --> 00:53:16,220
The people all around you long for you to believe,

997
00:53:16,220 --> 00:53:18,520
because as you change, and as you grow better,

998
00:53:18,520 --> 00:53:20,060
that is the very thing they long to see.

999
00:53:20,060 --> 00:53:21,340
And once you yourself believe,

1000
00:53:21,340 --> 00:53:26,200
they too can come to know the Lord through your own changed life in the days ahead.

1001
00:53:26,200 --> 00:53:30,560
So I'd like now to invite everyone who is willing to believe today to pray together with me, like this.

1002
00:53:30,800 --> 00:53:33,120
You may pray quietly in your own heart,

1003
00:53:33,360 --> 00:53:36,440
or you may pray along with me, phrase by phrase.

1004
00:53:37,200 --> 00:53:37,980
So let us now begin.

1005
00:53:41,820 --> 00:53:42,580
Lord Jesus,

1006
00:53:45,400 --> 00:53:47,440
I am willing to repent,

1007
00:53:49,240 --> 00:53:50,000
and to sin no more.

1008
00:53:52,320 --> 00:53:53,840
I ask You to forgive my whole life,

1009
00:53:54,880 --> 00:53:55,900
and all of my sins.

1010
00:53:56,200 --> 00:54:00,123
I am willing to receive You

1011
00:54:00,123 --> 00:54:04,700
as my own personal Savior.

1012
00:54:04,700 --> 00:54:09,340
This I sincerely pray.

1013
00:54:09,340 --> 00:54:16,920
And congratulations to every one of you who believed today and received the Lord as your Savior.

1014
00:54:16,920 --> 00:54:22,260
This year's Christmas will truly be an unforgettable one for you,

1015
00:54:22,260 --> 00:54:26,860
for you can now receive and enjoy all the things that God has prepared for you —

1016
00:54:27,120 --> 00:54:28,400
every blessing, and every happiness.
